{
  "title": "Scholarship Scheme Progress by District",
  "subtitle": "Overview of application status and pending cases across districts",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Applications",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Pending Cases",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Pending'",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Applications by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\", COUNT(*) AS total_apps FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10",
      "x": "district",
      "y": ["total_apps"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "stacked_bar",
      "title": "Status Breakdown by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\", SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Approved' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS approved, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Disbursed' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS disbursed, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Pending' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS pending, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Rejected' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS rejected, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Under Review' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS under_review FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY (approved + disbursed + pending + rejected + under_review) DESC LIMIT 10",
      "x": "district",
      "y": ["approved", "disbursed", "pending", "rejected", "under_review"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top Pending Cases by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\", COUNT(*) AS pending_count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Pending' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "This dashboard provides a comprehensive view of scholarship applications across different districts. The total number of applications is {{p1}}, with {{p2}} currently pending approval.\n\nThe bar chart highlights the distribution of applications by district, showing which areas have the highest volume of requests. This helps identify regions that may require additional support or resources.\n\nThe stacked bar chart breaks down the status of applications within each district, offering insights into how many are approved, disbursed, pending, rejected, or under review. This visualization aids in understanding the progress and bottlenecks in the scholarship process.\n\nFinally, the table lists the top districts with the most pending cases, enabling targeted interventions to expedite processing where needed."
}

{
  "title": "Child Fitness Improvement Dashboard",
  "subtitle": "Tracking physical progress from baseline to endline by location and coach",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Children Tracked",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"Child ID\") AS n FROM (SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"baseline\" UNION SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"endline\") AS all_children",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Shuttle Run Improvement (sec)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS n FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": "sec"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Sit Ups Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS n FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": "reps"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg Shuttle Run Change by Location",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Location\", AVG(e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_change FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 20",
      "x": "location",
      "y": ["avg_change"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg Sit Ups Change by Coach",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Coach\", AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS avg_change FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 20",
      "x": "coach",
      "y": ["avg_change"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top 10 Locations by Shuttle Run Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Location\", COUNT(*) AS child_count, AVG(e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 3 DESC LIMIT 10"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "This dashboard tracks the physical fitness progress of children from baseline to endline assessments. The total number of unique children tracked is {{p1}}. On average, children improved their shuttle run time by {{p2}} seconds, indicating better speed and agility. Additionally, the average increase in sit-ups was {{p3}} repetitions, showing enhanced core strength.\n\nThe bar chart by location highlights which areas saw the most significant improvements in shuttle run times, with the top performing locations leading the pack. Similarly, the coach-specific analysis reveals which instructors are driving the most substantial gains in core strength exercises.\n\nFor a detailed breakdown, the table lists the top 10 locations where children showed the greatest improvement in shuttle run performance, providing actionable insights for resource allocation and coaching strategies."
}

{
  "title": "Fitness Programme Impact Summary",
  "subtitle": "Overview of participant growth and performance changes from baseline to endline",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Participants",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"Child ID\") AS n FROM (SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"baseline\" UNION SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"endline\") AS all_ids",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg. Shuttle Run Improvement (sec)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS n FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": "sec"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg. Sit Ups Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS n FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": "reps"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg. Shuttle Run Time by Location",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Location\", AVG(\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_time FROM \"endline\" WHERE \"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 15",
      "x": "location",
      "y": ["avg_time"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg. Sit Ups by Coach",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Coach\", AVG(\"Sit ups\") AS avg_situps FROM \"endline\" WHERE \"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 15",
      "x": "coach",
      "y": ["avg_situps"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top Performers by Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Child name\", b.\"Location\", (e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS shuttle_diff, (e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS situps_diff FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL ORDER BY shuttle_diff ASC, situps_diff DESC LIMIT 10"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "This programme engaged {{p1}} children across multiple locations, tracking their physical development from baseline to endline. The data reveals a clear trend in endurance and strength, with participants showing an average improvement of {{p2}} seconds in the shuttle run test. \n\nStrength metrics also saw positive movement, with an average increase of {{p3}} sit-ups per child. These gains suggest the training regimen effectively targeted core stability and cardiovascular health. \n\nPerformance varied by location and coaching team, as seen in the breakdown of shuttle run times and sit-up averages. The top performers list highlights individuals who made the most significant strides, demonstrating the potential for high-impact outcomes when consistent attendance and coaching are maintained."
}

