      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top Overdue Loans by Amount",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Loan ID\", \"Block\", \"Purpose\", \"Loan Amount (Rs)\", \"Amount Repaid (Rs)\" FROM \"shg_loan_register\" WHERE \"Repayment Status\" = 'Overdue' ORDER BY \"Loan Amount (Rs)\" DESC LIMIT 10"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The SHG loan portfolio currently consists of {{p1}} total loans. Of these, {{p3}} loans are marked as overdue, indicating a need for closer monitoring.\n\nIn terms of financial recovery, the total amount repaid stands at {{p2}} Rs. This figure represents the cumulative sum of repayments from loans that are not in an overdue state.\n\nThe distribution of loans across different purposes reveals where capital is being directed. The bar chart highlights which sectors receive the highest funding volume.\n\nFinally, the table lists the top 10 overdue loans by principal amount, providing specific details on the blocks and purposes associated with the highest risk exposures."
}

{
  "title": "District Health Performance Dashboard",
  "subtitle": "Comparative analysis of key health indicators across districts in Bihar, Jharkhand, and Odisha",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Districts Analyzed",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"District\") AS n FROM \"district_health_factsheet\" WHERE \"District\" != 'State Total'",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg. Institutional Births",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(\"Institutional births (%)\") * 100 AS n FROM \"district_health_factsheet\" WHERE \"District\" != 'State Total'",
      "unit": "%"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg. Child Vaccination",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(\"Children age 12-23 months fully vaccinated (%)\") * 100 AS n FROM \"district_health_factsheet\" WHERE \"District\" != 'State Total'",
      "unit": "%"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Institutional Births by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\" AS district, \"Institutional births (%)\") * 100 AS inst_births FROM \"district_health_factsheet\" WHERE \"District\" != 'State Total' ORDER BY inst_births DESC LIMIT 20",
      "x": "district",
      "y": ["inst_births"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Child Stunting Rates by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\" AS district, \"Children under 5 years who are stunted (%)\") * 100 AS stunting_rate FROM \"district_health_factsheet\" WHERE \"District\" != 'State Total' ORDER BY stunting_rate DESC LIMIT 20",
      "x": "district",
      "y": ["stunting_rate"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "District Health Summary",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\", \"State\", \"Survey Round\", \"Institutional births (%)\") * 100 AS inst_births, \"Children age 12-23 months fully vaccinated (%)\") * 100 AS vaccination, \"Children under 5 years who are stunted (%)\") * 100 AS stunting FROM \"district_health_factsheet\" WHERE \"District\" != 'State Total' ORDER BY \"State\", \"District\""
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "This dashboard provides a comparative view of health outcomes across {{p1}} districts. The average rate of institutional births stands at {{p2}}, indicating the level of access to maternal healthcare facilities. Similarly, the average vaccination coverage for children aged 12-23 months is {{p3}}.\n\nThe bar charts highlight disparities between districts. Some districts show significantly higher institutional birth rates, while others lag behind, suggesting a need for targeted interventions. Stunting rates also vary, with certain districts facing higher malnutrition challenges.\n\nThe summary table offers a detailed breakdown, allowing for a deeper dive into specific district performance across key indicators. This data is crucial for policymakers to allocate resources effectively and improve overall public health outcomes."
}

